# Normalise line endings: store text as LF in the repository and check it out as
# LF on every platform, including Windows.
#
# Without this, a Windows checkout rewrites text files to CRLF. That caused two
# real problems here:
#   - `npm run format:check` and `npm run lint` failed, because prettier rejects
#     the stray CR ("Delete `␍`"), so a correct tree looked broken.
#   - An edit to public/budget/app.js showed up as a whole-file rewrite
#     (7000+ changed lines for a 175-line change), burying the real diff.
#
# `text=auto` lets git detect binary content and leave it alone; `eol=lf` forces
# LF on checkout so the working tree matches what is stored. This also overrides
# any local core.autocrlf setting.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binaries are never line-ending translated. `text=auto` already detects these,
# but naming them keeps a mis-detection from corrupting an asset.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.webp binary
*.avif binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.eot binary
*.pdf binary
*.zip binary
*.gz binary
*.mp3 binary
*.mp4 binary
